  "thumbnailAlt": "Conference Registration form beside a photo of an audience watching a speaker on a lit conference stage",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A conference registration form is a form that collects each attendee's contact and company details, pass type, the days and sessions they plan to attend, and any dietary or access needs so organizers can plan rooms, catering and badges. This template handles a multi-day event in three short pages, with session picks you can count before the doors open.",
    "audience": "Conference organizers, professional associations, user-group meetups, academic societies and corporate event teams running one- to three-day events.",
    "useCases": [
      "Annual industry conference with a workshop day and two main-stage days",
      "Academic symposium where attendees choose parallel tracks",
      "Internal company summit that needs headcounts per day for catering",
      "Developer conference that offers student and speaker passes"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Use conditional logic to show the workshop question only to people who pick the workshop day, so single-day attendees see a shorter form.",
      "Turn on the email plugin with the attendee's email as the recipient so every registrant gets a copy of their choices for their records.",
      "Set up a PDF template to generate a filled confirmation or name-badge PDF for each registration."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a conference registration form include?",
        "answer": "Name, email, job title and organization, pass type, which days the person will attend, their session or track choices, dietary and accessibility needs, the name to print on their badge, and any documents they need such as an invoice or visa letter."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I find out how many people want each session?",
        "answer": "Ask for session choices with a checkbox question. The response analytics show a chart for each question, so you can see how many attendees picked each track and size rooms to match."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I stop registrations when the venue is full?",
        "answer": "Yes. In Form Settings you can set a response limit and a closing date and time, and the form stops accepting registrations once either is reached."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does this form sell tickets?",
        "answer": "No. It records registrations only. If your conference charges a fee, collect it through your ticketing or invoicing tool and use the form for attendee details and session planning."
      }
    ]
  },
